2186045443 true] [17592186526358 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526358 1077 "selection" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526358 1078 #edb/ref 17592186526328 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526358 1079 #uuid "d79be9bf-c9f6-5c09-ae73-79dd5fda1afa" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526359 1080 "images/ca/ca18948802d9d78a214c7fe1c311b070dd75cb34cf1a86e419a11327dce67c6a.png" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526359 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526359 1083 #uuid "e51273cd-2b6f-50e1-87c1-939e753b8e95" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526360 1068 #edb/ref 17592186526346 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526360 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526360 1071 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5}{2}-(3)xy?$" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526360 1072 #uuid "e6247f84-7d87-51dd-98a1-cd1a03e15bc0" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526360 1074 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(1,-1)$,$(0,-2)$,$(-2,2)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,-1)}=\\frac{5}{2}-3(1)(-1)=\\frac{5}{2}-(-3)=\\frac{11}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-2)}=\\frac{5}{2}-3(0)(-2)=\\frac{5}{2}-(0)=\\frac{5}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,2)}=\\frac{5}{2}-3(-2)(2)=\\frac{5}{2}-(-12)=\\frac{29}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/f7/f77d4f1780e4ff74fce5e0303564f38a77968bd2e56390603a9b5b97f03b39a9.png)" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526361 1068 #edb/ref 17592186526319 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526361 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526361 1071 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}x^{2}-(-1)y^{2}?$" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526361 1072 #uuid "ec562691-61f7-5234-8201-f633bff4db89" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526361 1074 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,-1)$,$(2,-2)$,$(-1,3)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=\\frac{1}{2}(-2)^{2}-(-1)(-1)^{2}=2-(-1)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}-(-1)(-2)^{2}=2-(-4)=6, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)(3)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}-(-9)=\\frac{19}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/7a/7a323280b383e42c19701d86c4b005a769ae33539b380fa72e74b117629daac3.png)" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526362 1080 "images/38/38321f6b03143f9dc71efafa9be23d756bc3ae8f44eaaa114b67cff1d5cb7f5b.png" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526362 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526362 1083 #uuid "f2573c4a-1006-56c0-b90a-1c9782cd7914" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526363 1080 "images/15/1520124880f8f1a1f62b5f32f1d8d279234d3e539bdf1650aced55d25dab7a40.png" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526363 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526363 1083 #uuid "f33c98fd-0532-5521-8689-d95b9e3629f4" 13194139535696 17592186045443 true] [17592186526364 1080 "images/00/00be9e7ec3d6c5bb9b4e44423f6d84fe6db1073248d6e6c4767ff32cfc4deb84.png" 13194139535696 175921